BT /F2 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 755.00 Tm (THE BIG MONEY PLAYBOOKS) Tj ET
0.6 w 54.00 747.00 m 558.00 747.00 l S
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (exports. Use explicit connect and read timeouts supported by the chosen client, bounded retry attempts, randomized) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (backoff, and idempotent writes. For concurrency beyond a single local operator, use a managed database and tested) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (backups rather than sharing a live SQLite file through a consumer synchronization folder.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (Design failure handling around money and field safety, not uptime vanity. Poll hazard feeds at a documented,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (service-appropriate cadence, but let the provider's caching guidance and response headers govern actual retrieval. On) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (HTTP 429, honor Retry-After when present; on authentication failure, stop the connector and alert its owner instead of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (repeatedly submitting credentials. Paginate deterministically and preserve a checkpoint only after the local transaction) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (commits. For webhook integrations, verify the vendor's documented authentication mechanism, persist the event) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (identifier, acknowledge promptly, and process through an idempotent worker. Treat duplicate delivery and out-of-order) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (updates as normal conditions. A payment webhook must not erase a newer accounting adjustment merely because it) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm (arrived later. Route unrecoverable records to a review queue with source, attempted operation, and a safe error message) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.52 Tm (that excludes credentials and unnecessary personal data. Set different freshness tolerances for weather, licenses,) Tj ET
