BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (capacity. Engage genuine independent businesses for bounded scopes, subject to applicable worker-classification tests.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (A contractor label cannot cure an employment relationship, and continuous employee-like supervision is a warning) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (requiring classification review. Use purchase orders stating quantities, authorized rates, evidence requirements,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (exclusions, and change-order authority. For example, a separately priced plumbing isolation task does not include) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (reconstruction or permission to expand demolition. Pay accepted milestones under the written terms and applicable) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (prompt-payment rules rather than making payment contingent on an insurer's reimbursement. Schedule two daily) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (handoff windows, preserve emergency escalation, and avoid pretending that eleven people provide unlimited overnight) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (coverage. Route overflow to a prequalified referral partner without representing their workforce as the pod's own) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (capacity. Safety-critical work, electrical isolation, regulated remediation, and containment design remain) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (qualification-based assignments; a cheaper available technician is not an interchangeable substitute for the required) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm (specialist on a hazardous property.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.52 Tm (At the Scaled case, add one full-time restoration operations supervisor and one qualified remediation contractor,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 533.30 Tm (creating six employees plus seven contractors. The supervisor takes daily production coordination and field exception) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 518.07 Tm (resolution from the owner; the seventh contractor increases specialist availability rather than automatically increasing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 502.85 Tm (every trade's throughput. Release this expansion only after a rolling thirteen-week capacity plan identifies the actual) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 487.62 Tm (bottleneck and a cash forecast funds payroll, vendor commitments, and equipment without counting disputed) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 472.40 Tm (supplements. Keep the canonical cases intact: $500,000 at 8% produces $40,000 owner profit; $1,500,000 at 13.0%) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 457.17 Tm (produces $195,000; $2,500,000 at 18% produces $450,000. Their implied total annual costs are $460,000, $1,305,000,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 441.95 Tm (and $2,050,000 respectively. Those totals must absorb the modeled labor, subcontracting, materials, equipment,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 426.72 Tm (overhead, and other costs behind each net margin. The Conservative case leaves little room for five market-rate) Tj ET
